WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.160
Once again, it's time to fire up the Mighty
Marvel rumor mill.

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:09.140
Pop culture website We Got This Covered is
reporting that its wily, ever-anonymous sources

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:13.900
have knowledge that Marvel Studios is eyeing
Dacre Montgomery, who portrayed Billy Hargrove

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:18.070
on the hit Netflix series Stranger Things,
to fill the role of Wolverine in the Marvel

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:19.200
Cinematic Universe.

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:23.520
Before we go any further, we feel compelled
to make a few things clear about this "breaking"

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:24.020
news.

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:28.820
First, WGTC is typically not a super-reliable
source of inside information.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:33.680
While the website has fielded accurate rumor
reports in the past, it also has a pesky habit

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:35.420
of spreading absolute malarkey.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:39.420
Plus, since no other media outlets are reporting
that Marvel wants the young Australian actor

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:43.980
for the role of Wolverine, the idea that these
folks are "breaking" anything but Dacre Montgomery

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.920
fans' hearts is pretty laughable.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:50.840
"I have never felt such humor!"

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:57.680
Second, this isn't the first time Montgomery
has been connected to a Marvel role by the

00:00:57.740 --> 00:00:58.240
fandom.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:02.760
As recently as last summer, the same website
reported that he was being considered for

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:07.860
the part of Adam Warlock in James Gunn's upcoming
Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3, for example.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:12.060
We'll leave it to you to decide whether this
indicates that Marvel Studios is trying super-hard

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:16.110
to find the right role for the talented actor,
or that the internet's rumor mongers stepped

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:17.540
on their own feet with this one.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:22.260
Third: if indeed Marvel is considering Montgomery
to take on the role of Wolverine which, again,

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:26.080
it could honestly go either way we're basically
as on board as you could get.

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:30.009
Ever since we got our hands on the actor's
insane Stranger Things audition tape, we've

00:01:30.009 --> 00:01:33.200
wanted to see him land a major role in a superhero
franchise.

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:37.600
"OK, now listen: Why don't you put that away
before you shoot yourself in the foot with

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:38.260
it, OK?

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:39.880
You ain't got the sack to shoot a woodchuck."

00:01:40.229 --> 00:01:44.320
We literally can't think of a better fit for
him than everyone's favorite cigar-chomping,

00:01:44.329 --> 00:01:48.799
adamantium-infused mutant especially after
we saw our favorite digital artist BossLogic's

00:01:48.799 --> 00:01:49.840
rendition of the guy!

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:55.329
As psyched as we would be to see Montgomery
take over as Logan in the MCU, WGTC's alleged

00:01:55.329 --> 00:02:00.100
inside sources also put forth a small addendum
to the rumor which makes us doubt the whole

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:00.600
shebang.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:04.820
According to them, Marvel brass are still
hopeful that they might be able to coax Hugh

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:08.899
Jackman, who held down the role for almost
20 years in the Fox Studios-produced X-Men

00:02:08.899 --> 00:02:10.099
movies, to return.

00:02:10.099 --> 00:02:14.700
Failing that, the sources say, the studio
would then be interested in talking to Montgomery.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:17.440
Pardon us for saying so, but this doesn't
make a lick of sense.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:22.080
When the X-Men and especially Wolverine finally
join the MCU, Marvel is going to want them

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:25.600
to be cast with actors who are capable of
playing their respective roles for as long

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:26.340
as possible.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:31.331
At 51, this would in no way describe Jackman,
who in any event has stated plainly that he

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:32.300
is done with the role.

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:37.040
Montgomery is only 25, so if this rumor is
true, it indicates that Marvel just isn't

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:39.599
sure whether they want to go with an older
or a younger Logan.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:42.640
We ask you: does this sound like Marvel Studios,
like, at all?

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:46.300
This is the studio which has a rough sketch
of its shared universe mapped out through

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:49.420
2028, according to head honcho Kevin Feige.

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:53.159
We're pretty sure that plans are well underway
for the introduction of the X-Men to the Marvel

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:57.280
Cinematic Universe, and that no actors of
Jackman's vintage will be sought for the primary

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:57.780
roles.

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:01.820
It's worth mentioning that Montgomery has
previously appeared hesitant to star in comic

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:03.080
book movies in general.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:08.120
In a 2019 video for GQ's "Actually Me" series,
in which the actor went undercover on social

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:12.459
media to take part in discussions about himself,
he encountered a fan who suggested that he'd

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:17.160
be perfect for the part of Jason Todd — AKA
Red Hood — the iconic Batman sidekick turned

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:17.660
villain.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:19.620
Montgomery's response was pretty thoughtful.

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:20.800
He said, in part:

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:26.340
"I would really like to play outside of the
world that's so prominent, I guess, in cinemas

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:30.300
at the moment, which is just origin stories
of amazing superheroes that we love."

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:34.420
He added that he'd love to, quote, " … dive
into a different world that we don't know,

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:35.200
that we aren't...

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:35.920
given a lot of."

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:39.760
Whether it turns out that Montgomery's got
the gusto to play Ol' Canucklehead or not,

00:03:39.769 --> 00:03:43.640
we'll be keeping both ears to the ground for
any news regarding the future of the X-Men

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:46.820
in the MCU — and, as always, we'll keep
you informed.

